From c9f31c3a3cbfa05b511b907793a578d8ebf8b13a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH] Desugar the for loops of the analyzed code into while let

`for x in e` is written as `let mut it = e.into_iter(); while let Some(x)
= it.next()`, which is what the compiler produces; where `e` is already
an iterator the blanket IntoIterator (the identity) is skipped. The loops
of the trusted univariant_biased are left alone. This exposes the
iterator calls to Thrust without std's IntoIterator bodies; the iterated
expressions, including the std adapters (enumerate, IterMut, IntoIter),
are unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/main.rs | 24 ++++++++++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

